WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:11.120
Will there be a meatless burger in your
future? It's not impossible! In 2018, total

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.570
sales of substitute meat products were
already estimated to be about 4.5

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.500
billion dollars, and McDonald's recently
announced that it will test-market a

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.570
burger that uses plant proteins instead
of beef. But going forward, companies like

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.609
Beyond Meat may have trouble finding the
dry peas they need to make patties. The

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:36.840
good news: 1.1 million acres were planted
in 2019. The bad news: Switching from

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.860
traditional crops to dry peas will
involve equipment changes, and may

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.059
require some farms to gain experience
working with the new crop, adding costs

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:49.050
and time. And another barrier exists for
companies that insist on using organic

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:54.000
peas. Under current USDA rules, it takes
three years to qualify land to raise

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.699
certified organic crops. But if all goes
well, plant-based meat sales could double

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:05.480
by 2024, and might account for 20% of all
meat sales in a few decades.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.420
Would you buy a fast-food, meatless burger? Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:17.670
what other topics you would like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:23.869
sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

